  <div class="about__text">
    <h2 id="about-h" class="display glitch" data-text="About me" data-reveal>About me</h2>
    <p data-reveal style="--d:1">I was a writer before I was a developer. I built worlds first: universes, power systems, characters with flaws they can’t outrun. Then I found code, and started building things that run instead of things you read.</p>
    <p data-reveal style="--d:2">Now I’m a third-year IT student at Saint Louis University, still figuring a lot of it out. I like building for problems people actually have, like a blood donation app for my web class, or KitaKlaro, a tool for small businesses that went from a pitch to a working prototype.</p>
    <p data-reveal style="--d:3">The worldbuilding never left. It’s why I think in systems, rules and edge cases, and why I care how something feels to use. Next, I’m learning AI engineering properly, from the ground up.</p>
  </div>
